-- SessionRuntimeEvent(type='text_delta', data={'content': 'Verification passed.
Summary of the change:\n\n**`src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx`**\n- Extracted the 
120 ms simulated sync into a shared `schedule(next)` helper backed by a single 
`timerRef`, plus `clearTimer` for unmount cleanup (preserving the original 
cleanup behavior).\n- The mount effect still reads `?sync=` once and resolves to
`error` or `success` exactly as before, so `/` is unchanged.\n- Added a `Retry 
sync` button inside the error alert. Its handler immediately sets `loading` and 
schedules the same 120 ms transition to `success`; it returns early if a timer 
is already pending, so repeated activation cannot create overlapping timers. The
button renders only in the `error` state and so disappears on success. No 
navigation/reload or state reset — the selected task lives outside this 
component and `window.location` is never touched.\n\n**`src/styles.css`**\n- 
Added `.sync-retry { justify-self: start; margin-top: 8px; }` so the recovery 
action sits below the error copy, reusing the existing `button.secondary` style 
and existing focus-visible outline rules.\n\n**Commands actually run:** 
`verify_frontend` → `npm run build` (tsc + vite, success) and `npm run 
test:public` (Playwright, 6/6 passed). No existing tests were 
modified.\n\n**Remaining risks:** the retry path has no public test (only the 
success state does), so its behavior is verified by reasoning rather than an 
automated assertion; if a future test asserts a different delay constant, the 
shared `SYNC_DELAY` would be the single place to change. The guard relies on 
React\'s single-threaded click handling, which is adequate for this "no 
overlapping timers" requirement.', 'aid': 0})
